menu "Gateway: storage"

    config GW_CONFIG_MAX_BYTES
        int "Largest accepted /cfg/config.json (bytes)"
        range 4096 1048576
        default 131072
        help
            The spec maximum (16 devices, 256 tags with every field) is about 46 KB of
            compact JSON and 82 KB indented with 2 spaces. The file and the parser's
            document tree (about 200 KB for 256 tags) are allocated at boot, in PSRAM
            when present, and freed before the gateway starts. A larger file is
            rejected: the gateway then stays stopped with the configuration error state.

endmenu
